# Chains of Mephistopheles and Laboratory Maniac both replace a draw Bot1 would make from an empty library outside the first
# of its draw step, and Bot1 chooses which applies first (CR 616.1). Its library's last card is drawn in its turn 3 draw step
# (the step's first card: Chains leaves it alone, and the library still had it, so Laboratory Maniac does too). Ancestral
# Recall's first draw then finds the library empty: Bot1 applies Laboratory Maniac, and wins the game instead of drawing
# (CR 104.2b) - it discards nothing, as Chains never applied.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Chains of Mephistopheles
Laboratory Maniac
Ancestral Recall
Forest
Plains

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Laboratory Maniac.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Library.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Replace(Laboratory Maniac)

[Expect]
Result = Bot1 won
Bot2.Status = Lost
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Plains
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
